\ Deadline: the people. Each person has a number (:character): 0 the
\ player, 1 McNabb the gardener, 2 Baxter, 3 Dunbar, 4 George, 5 Mrs.
\ Robner, 6 Mrs. Rourke, 7 Coates. A person out of the room is spoken of
\ through a global counterpart present everywhere, and last-seen holds for
\ each person the time each other person was last seen with them.

[ :player :gardener :baxter :dunbar :george :mrs-robner :rourke :coates ] to character-table

[ :player :global-gardener :global-baxter :global-dunbar :global-george
  :global-mrs-robner :global-rourke :global-coates
] to global-character-table

7 constant character-max

[ ""
  "Mr. McNabb is an elderly Scottish man with a deeply lined face. He is
  wearing overalls."
  "Baxter is an immaculately dressed middle-aged man with rugged good looks."
  "Ms. Dunbar, wearing a fashionable pants suit, is a rather attractive woman
  in her early thirties."
  "George is a young man in his mid-twenties. He is poorly dressed in that
  each item he is wearing clashes with the others. His attire is of the
  highest quality, however. He is wearing various pieces of jewelry."
  "Mrs. Robner is a middle-aged woman of great beauty. She is dressed in
  black."
  "Mrs. Rourke is a short woman, more than a bit overweight. She is wearing a
  maid's outfit."
  "Mr. Coates is a rather homely man of advancing years."
] to character-descriptions

\ the time each person last saw each other person, 0 for never
[ 0 8 array-of 0 8 array-of 0 8 array-of 0 8 array-of
  0 8 array-of 0 8 array-of 0 8 array-of 0 8 array-of
] to last-seen

\ the person a character number stands for, and the global counterpart
: character ( n -- name ) character-table swap @i ;

: global-character ( n -- name ) global-character-table swap @i ;
